<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Standard layout w/ ACS, lots of addenda to expand on the concept, short testing logs and an incident report.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> It has the appearance of an ATM machine, with a glass front screen and 2 buttons on the ATM's base where the keypad normally is; the left button is red, and the right button is blue. The card reader slot on a normal ATM machine is used to insert a piece of paper/papyrus, and then a button can be pressed. Red will paint an image where someone close to the person who activated it is depicted doing something (anything can be pictured), and the Foundation does not want anybody to know what the blue button does, since it does something so veil-breaking.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The story will be carried through an incident report, an interview log, testing logs, and addenda. The addenda will show how much the Foundation tried to keep the item secret, and prohibit any activation of the blue button. They started to implement procedures to try and keep it from being abused, and then after they did that, they opened it up again, but they still need to keep the blue button as a last resort.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The story will be carried in-depth, and the mystery of what the second button will do and why it's so important to keep it even though it will be veil-breaking.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> This idea has been in my head for a while, and I just wanted to get it out there.</p>

