<p>Solid concept, good execution, but the numbers are too off, that break it to me.</p>
<p>A velocity of 10&#160;m/s is just 36 Km/h (less than 22.5 miles/hour), terminal velocity for a pine cone isn't much more than throwing them by hand, and the force of the explosion wasn't given. So, as far as I'm aware, this isn't nearly as dangerous as it is purported to be.</p>
<p>It isn't Keter, either. Even if you make it more dangerous than a modern ICBM its containment is quite reliable, and I see no reason to be otherwise. This is a solid Euclid.</p>
<p>You don't need to make this more dangerous. You can correct the numbers to really make it into a war-worthy missile, or you can go with the numbers and make it a freak flying tree with annoying dropping cones and a somewhat dangerous blast at the end. It works either way, if not better with the current low numbers.</p>

							</div>

								
					
